#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Omarchy Music: a minimal music popup, themed live from Omarchy.

Browse and search YouTube Music, Tidal, Apple Music or Spotify (switch at the
top), and the music in your own folders (~/Music to start). The audio of the
services always comes from Tidal in FLAC (hi-res where Tidal has it): each
song is matched there (by its ISRC when the service has one, else by title,
artist and length) and streamed. Download (the FLAC mark by the controls, or
a song's menu) saves it to play from disk. Nothing downloads on its own: "Keep"
in the accounts menu saves every song you play, and each service has a Sync
switch that saves all of its playlists, all off to start. Apple Music's own
audio is locked with DRM, so its songs play from the same recording on Tidal.
Songs Tidal has no lossless copy of are skipped. The next song in the queue
is looked up ahead so tracks change without a wait.

The Music tab has all your songs (downloaded and in your folders), your own
playlists, and what you played recently, added recently and play most. Click
an artist's name for their page. Right-click a song (or select several) to
queue it or add it to a playlist. The window takes its colour from the album
art. Saved songs are tagged in the background (genre, composer, label,
MusicBrainz IDs, a big cover, lyrics), plays are scrobbled to Last.fm, the
Lyrics tab shows Genius's lyrics (or lines timed to the music), and Wrapped
looks back on any week, month or year of your Last.fm history (or all of it).

The Android app (android/ in the repository) does all of this on a phone, and
can play here instead: switch on "Phone" in the accounts menu and pair the
phone with the code it shows. The phone then shows what's playing here and
every play, queue and button press goes to this app. The remote listens on
port 8897 of your network (allow it in your firewall) and is off to start.

  omarchy-music                     open, or toggle the popup if it is already running
  omarchy-music play SONG...        play now: a search, a link or a file ("-": one per line of stdin)
  omarchy-music next SONG...        play right after the current song
  omarchy-music queue SONG...       add to the queue, after the songs you queued before
  omarchy-music play | pause | skip | prev    without a song: the transport
  omarchy-music lyrics [genius|synced]   show the lyrics of what's playing (as written, or timed)
  omarchy-music search WORDS...     open the popup on a search
  omarchy-music show [TAB]          open the popup on search, library, music, playlists, recent,
                                    added, top, queue or lyrics
  omarchy-music accounts            the accounts menu: sign-ins, folders, Last.fm, the tagger
  omarchy-music wrapped [YEAR|month|week|all]   your year (month, week or every year) in music,
                                    from your Last.fm history
  omarchy-music source youtube|tidal|apple|spotify   switch the library you browse and search
  omarchy-music tag [all]           tag the saved songs not tagged yet (or all of them) now
  omarchy-music status              what's playing, what's next, how far the tagging is
  omarchy-music quit                stop the music and quit
  omarchy-music --tidal-login       connect Tidal from a terminal (the accounts menu can too)
  omarchy-music --lastfm-login      connect Last.fm from a terminal (the accounts menu can too)
  omarchy-music --spotify-login     connect Spotify from a terminal (the accounts menu can too)
  Commands run while it isn't running start it in the background first.
  Files: ~/Music/Omarchy Music/  (songs/ with a .lrc of timed lyrics beside each song, art/,
         library.json, playlists.json, missing.json); logins in ~/.local/state/omarchy-music-*.json

Media keys work through MPRIS (playerctl); mpv does the playback.
"""
